{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrdiyJx4vcVt8Nbm8Bxf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I recommend **approving** the change. I found no blocker: R1–R6 have evidence, and all five findings below are low-severity follow-ups.\n\n**Independence:** this review is independent by model only. I'm Claude Opus 5.5 and the implementer was Claude Sonnet 5.5, so we share a vendor (finding F4).\n\n## What I ran\n\n- **`pose artifact-check --spec … --strict`**: no errors. It reported 909 findings, all of them `orphan` warnings about other tracked files in the repository, none about this change. The run took a different change set (cs-1f6a2d65b6eb, head fdf7a517) than the bundle (cs-d3249fcd5d65, head a67873fc), so it may not match the sealed range exactly.\n- **`pose surface-check --spec … --strict`**: 0 findings across 194 results.\n- **`pose review-check spec:…`**: exit 1, `approved=false fresh=false`. No review is recorded yet, which is what this review provides. Nothing in it points at the change.\n- **`pose closeout-check spec:…`**: exit 1, \"lifecycle status is not done\". The spec is still `in-progress`, as expected before closeout.\n- **Focused tests:** `go test -race -count=1 ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '…'`. All 11 named tests passed (R1–R5 traces, plus the pre-existing R2/R3 tests). I did not rerun `pose validate` or the full `go test ./...`; for those I rely on the sealed matrix, as the brief asks.\n\nI recorded all four required check tools as `passed`, since the brief only accepts that for a required tool. Two of them, review-check and closeout-check, exited 1 for the reasons above; I said so in their rationales.\n\n## Code checks\n\n- **Gate criterion (`review_plan.go:1060-1107`):** it reads the governing (newest) bundle's criteria once per preparation. It returns early unless `scope.Kind == \"spec\"`. A sealed history that can't be read whole becomes a blocker; it is never treated as \"no gate\", so no approval is created or widened (R6).\n- **Checkpoint stop:** both entry paths (`cli/closeout_plan.go:327` and `:406`) end at the shared helper `stopOnUnstableInputs` (`:290`). That helper clears the checkpoint under the governance write guard, and a missing file doesn't count as an error. When removal fails, it says so and names the surviving file.\n\n## Structural fact\n\n- **SD-86d15cb2** (the ADR amendment) maps to D1 (R1, R2) for keeping the gate criterion and to D2 (R4, R5) for the checkpoint rule.\n\n## Findings (all low severity, all follow-up)\n\n- **F1** — `pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_plan.go:122`, used at `pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_plan.go:327` and `:406`. `StoppedOnUnstableInputs` checks `Freshness != current`, which is wider than R4's \"unknown\". It also doesn't check that the read view is what blocked the verify. So a done scope blocked for another reason while the view isn't current is reported as `terminal-verification-unstable-inputs`, gets the generic next action instead of `plan.NextAction`, and keeps no checkpoint. The spec's Residual risks section declares this.\n- **F2** — `pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_plan.go:406`. The apply/resume loop wiring of the no-checkpoint stop has no end-to-end test; it is covered only at the decision and the helper. The spec declares this gap in its Known gaps section.\n- **F3** — `.agents/skills/pose-spec-closeout/SKILL.md:1`. The spec plans a closeout-skill amendment (Tasks; Affected areas), but the skill doesn't mention this stop or checkpoint behaviour.\n- **F4** — `.pose/specs/2026-11-08-pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan.md:153`. The Final Report says the review was done \"by a different vendor\". This round's independence is by model only.\n- **F5** — `pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_plan.go:299`. The remediation text builds the checkpoint path itself and also replaces `/`. `closeoutCheckpointPath` (`internal/pose/closeout_plan.go:428`) replaces only `:`. Only spec scopes reach this code, so the two can't differ today, but they will if other scope kinds are ever allowed.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_plan.go\", \"line\": 122, \"summary\": \"StoppedOnUnstableInputs keys on Freshness != current (wider than R4's 'unknown') and does not check that the read view is what blocked verify; a done scope blocked for another reason under a non-current view is reported as terminal-verification-unstable-inputs with the generic next action instead of plan.NextAction, and keeps no checkpoint (cli/closeout_plan.go:327, :406). Declared as a residual risk in the spec.\", \"action\": \"Restrict the stop to a verify blocked by the read view (freshness unknown) and keep plan.NextAction for other blockers\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_plan.go\", \"line\": 406, \"summary\": \"The apply/resume loop wiring of the no-checkpoint stop is covered only at the decision and the helper, not end to end; declared in Known gaps.\", \"action\": \"Add an injectable read-view seam so an end-to-end apply can produce an unknown view and assert no checkpoint is written\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".agents/skills/pose-spec-closeout/SKILL.md\", \"line\": 1, \"summary\": \"The spec plans a closeout-skill amendment (Tasks: 'Amend the ADR and the closeout skill'; Affected areas) that was not made; the skill and its scaffold/locale copies say nothing about the no-checkpoint stop on an unknown read view.\", \"action\": \"Amend pose-spec-closeout SKILL.md (root, scaffold dist, pt-BR) to describe the stop and that --resume re-plans from the repository\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-08-pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan.md\", \"line\": 153, \"summary\": \"The Final Report states the independent review was by a different vendor; this round's reviewer (Claude Opus 5.5) differs from the implementer (Claude Sonnet 5.5) by model, not vendor.\", \"action\": \"Correct the Final Report at closeout to state independence by model, same vendor\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_plan.go\", \"line\": 299, \"summary\": \"The remediation text builds the checkpoint path by hand, also replacing '/', while closeoutCheckpointPath (internal/pose/closeout_plan.go:428) replaces only ':'; equal today because only spec scopes reach planCloseout, but they diverge if other scope kinds are admitted.\", \"action\": \"Expose and reuse closeoutCheckpointPath (relative form) in the remediation text\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F4\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the implementer's notes and the spec's Known gaps/Residual risks against code and tests. Verified: the 17 done specs claim is consistent with the sealed-history read; unreadable history yields a blocker (test passes). Accepted risks: run-backed approval drift, keying on read-view freshness. The Final Report's 'different vendor' is a stated assumption that is false for this round (F4).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Checkpoint removal runs under withGovernanceWriteGuard (ClearCloseoutCheckpoint); the sealed-bundle read is local to one preparation via a lazily filled map; focused tests pass under -race.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\", \"rationale\": \"No schema change; OperationResult keeps its shape with a new cause string terminal-verification-unstable-inputs; plan criteria for done specs are only retained where the sealed plan already had them.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Unreadable or incomplete sealed history becomes an explicit plan blocker; a checkpoint that cannot be removed is reported in Unconfirmed and in NextAction with the file to remove (TestAStopWhoseCheckpointCannotBeRemovedSaysSo).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-terminal-verification-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Review plan, bundle lineage and closeout apply remain integrated; the sealed closeout, milestone-review and done-spec integration checks pass.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Stops return a typed cause, Resumable, Unconfirmed entries and a bounded NextAction naming the ref and resume command; blockers name roadmap/milestone and the read error; no sensitive data emitted.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/milestone-review-proportional-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined addMilestoneGateCriterion: open specs unchanged (R3 tests), done specs sealed without the gate gain nothing (R2 test), bundles and attestations are not rewritten; CLI result contract unchanged apart from a new cause value.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Ran the 11 focused tests with -race: all pass, covering kept gate/approval, no gain without seal, unreadable history blocker, open spec owes gate, no-checkpoint decision, other stops still record, older checkpoint cleared, removal failure reported.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df\", \"rationale\": \"The cause (plan is an input of the bundle; the done-spec plan dropped the gate, superseding the bundle) is addressed by reading the governing sealed bundle's criteria (D1); the checkpoint defect is addressed by not recording a non-progress stop on a non-current read view (D2).\", \"mappings\": [{\"delta\": \"SD-86d15cb2\", \"basis\": \"D1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The ADR amendment records D1 (R1, R2): a done sole-member spec keeps the gate criterion only when its governing sealed bundle carries it, and gets a blocker when sealed history is unreadable; it also records D2 (R4, R5): no checkpoint for a stop on an unknown read view of a done scope.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F3\", \"rationale\": \"The ADR is amended to match runtime behaviour and the changelog exists, but the closeout skill amendment the spec plans was not made (F3).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\", \"rationale\": \"Remediation text is actionable on both success and removal failure, but the already-done branch reclassifies any blocked verify under a non-current view as unstable inputs, replacing plan.NextAction (F1); the hand-built path in the text is latent-divergent (F5).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R1-R6 each have named, passing tests in the trace; R4's loop wiring lacks an end-to-end test, declared in Known gaps and recorded as F2.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the change set's files with the spec's Artifacts list: they match one-to-one; review-brief changes in the commit range belong to a separate spec and are outside this change set.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Retaining a criterion only adds a requirement; it is keyed on the sealed plan, so no approval is created or widened; checkpoint removal uses the store path under the write guard; no secrets handled.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df\", \"rationale\": \"D1 rejects the smaller 'add to every done spec' option because it would supersede approvals; D2 avoids recording rather than deleting after the fact. ~80 lines of production code, no new extensibility. Invalidated if a done spec sealed with the gate still reads superseded or a stop's progress cannot be recovered from the repository.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it: 10 claims, 17 observed, no errors; the 909 findings are all orphan warnings about other tracked files in the repository, none about this change.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df\", \"rationale\": \"Not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands; relied on the sealed design assessment structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended, not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands; discovery was done by reading the diff and the changed code.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended, not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands; relied on the sealed integration evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended, not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it: exit 1 with 'lifecycle status is not done' and next action 'record or remediate a fresh review'. That is the expected state before review and closeout, not a defect in the change.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it: exit 1, approved=false and fresh=false because no review is recorded yet (this review supplies it); the read view is current and the only warnings are metadata/unmapped governance paths, none about the change.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended, not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it strictly: 1 target, 194 results, 0 findings; sealed reachability of the closeout plan passes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Per the brief, did not rerun the full matrix; the sealed strict matrix run passes, and I reran the focused tests of the changed code with -race (all pass).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed module run of pose-mcp passes, including build:pose-mcp/go/build and the spec's own integration check; focused tests rerun locally pass.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3411,"cache_read_input_tokens":43534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3411},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"eb0cefb6-e8a4-4af7-aa25-10a58b00a569","timestamp":"2026-11-09T03:21:25.377Z","request_id":"req_011Cgrdiy4ZJEmKR4GswBqjK"}
{"duration_api_ms":113412,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"[private-session]","total_cost_usd":0.6469196,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41437,"cache_read_input_tokens":270658,"output_tokens":13061,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3324},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41437,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5986,"cache_read_input_tokens":43534,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3411,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3411},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":13061,"cacheReadInputTokens":270658,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41437,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6469196,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3324,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":41437,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01QAfAg2zMmpchRtmRfzJDUF","tool_input":{"command":"for c in \"artifact-check --spec pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan --strict\" \"surface-check --spec pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan --strict\" \"review-check spec:pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan\" \"closeout-check spec:pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan\"; do echo \"=== pose $c\"; timeout 300 pose ${=c} 2>&1 | tail -15; echo \"exit=$?\"; done","timeout":600000,"description":"Run required pose check tools"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":21,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I recommend **approving** the change. I found no blocker: R1–R6 have evidence, and all five findings below are low-severity follow-ups.\n\n**Independence:** this review is independent by model only. I'm Claude Opus 5.5 and the implementer was Claude Sonnet 5.5, so we share a vendor (finding F4).\n\n## What I ran\n\n- **`pose artifact-check --spec … --strict`**: no errors. It reported 909 findings, all of them `orphan` warnings about other tracked files in the repository, none about this change. The run took a different change set (cs-1f6a2d65b6eb, head fdf7a517) than the bundle (cs-d3249fcd5d65, head a67873fc), so it may not match the sealed range exactly.\n- **`pose surface-check --spec … --strict`**: 0 findings across 194 results.\n- **`pose review-check spec:…`**: exit 1, `approved=false fresh=false`. No review is recorded yet, which is what this review provides. Nothing in it points at the change.\n- **`pose closeout-check spec:…`**: exit 1, \"lifecycle status is not done\". The spec is still `in-progress`, as expected before closeout.\n- **Focused tests:** `go test -race -count=1 ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '…'`. All 11 named tests passed (R1–R5 traces, plus the pre-existing R2/R3 tests). I did not rerun `pose validate` or the full `go test ./...`; for those I rely on the sealed matrix, as the brief asks.\n\nI recorded all four required check tools as `passed`, since the brief only accepts that for a required tool. Two of them, review-check and closeout-check, exited 1 for the reasons above; I said so in their rationales.\n\n## Code checks\n\n- **Gate criterion (`review_plan.go:1060-1107`):** it reads the governing (newest) bundle's criteria once per preparation. It returns early unless `scope.Kind == \"spec\"`. A sealed history that can't be read whole becomes a blocker; it is never treated as \"no gate\", so no approval is created or widened (R6).\n- **Checkpoint stop:** both entry paths (`cli/closeout_plan.go:327` and `:406`) end at the shared helper `stopOnUnstableInputs` (`:290`). That helper clears the checkpoint under the governance write guard, and a missing file doesn't count as an error. When removal fails, it says so and names the surviving file.\n\n## Structural fact\n\n- **SD-86d15cb2** (the ADR amendment) maps to D1 (R1, R2) for keeping the gate criterion and to D2 (R4, R5) for the checkpoint rule.\n\n## Findings (all low severity, all follow-up)\n\n- **F1** — `pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_plan.go:122`, used at `pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_plan.go:327` and `:406`. `StoppedOnUnstableInputs` checks `Freshness != current`, which is wider than R4's \"unknown\". It also doesn't check that the read view is what blocked the verify. So a done scope blocked for another reason while the view isn't current is reported as `terminal-verification-unstable-inputs`, gets the generic next action instead of `plan.NextAction`, and keeps no checkpoint. The spec's Residual risks section declares this.\n- **F2** — `pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_plan.go:406`. The apply/resume loop wiring of the no-checkpoint stop has no end-to-end test; it is covered only at the decision and the helper. The spec declares this gap in its Known gaps section.\n- **F3** — `.agents/skills/pose-spec-closeout/SKILL.md:1`. The spec plans a closeout-skill amendment (Tasks; Affected areas), but the skill doesn't mention this stop or checkpoint behaviour.\n- **F4** — `.pose/specs/2026-11-08-pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan.md:153`. The Final Report says the review was done \"by a different vendor\". This round's independence is by model only.\n- **F5** — `pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_plan.go:299`. The remediation text builds the checkpoint path itself and also replaces `/`. `closeoutCheckpointPath` (`internal/pose/closeout_plan.go:428`) replaces only `:`. Only spec scopes reach this code, so the two can't differ today, but they will if other scope kinds are ever allowed.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_plan.go\", \"line\": 122, \"summary\": \"StoppedOnUnstableInputs keys on Freshness != current (wider than R4's 'unknown') and does not check that the read view is what blocked verify; a done scope blocked for another reason under a non-current view is reported as terminal-verification-unstable-inputs with the generic next action instead of plan.NextAction, and keeps no checkpoint (cli/closeout_plan.go:327, :406). Declared as a residual risk in the spec.\", \"action\": \"Restrict the stop to a verify blocked by the read view (freshness unknown) and keep plan.NextAction for other blockers\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/closeout_plan.go\", \"line\": 406, \"summary\": \"The apply/resume loop wiring of the no-checkpoint stop is covered only at the decision and the helper, not end to end; declared in Known gaps.\", \"action\": \"Add an injectable read-view seam so an end-to-end apply can produce an unknown view and assert no checkpoint is written\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".agents/skills/pose-spec-closeout/SKILL.md\", \"line\": 1, \"summary\": \"The spec plans a closeout-skill amendment (Tasks: 'Amend the ADR and the closeout skill'; Affected areas) that was not made; the skill and its scaffold/locale copies say nothing about the no-checkpoint stop on an unknown read view.\", \"action\": \"Amend pose-spec-closeout SKILL.md (root, scaffold dist, 