ition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Ran the 11 focused tests with -race: all pass, covering kept gate/approval, no gain without seal, unreadable history blocker, open spec owes gate, no-checkpoint decision, other stops still record, older checkpoint cleared, removal failure reported.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df\", \"rationale\": \"The cause (plan is an input of the bundle; the done-spec plan dropped the gate, superseding the bundle) is addressed by reading the governing sealed bundle's criteria (D1); the checkpoint defect is addressed by not recording a non-progress stop on a non-current read view (D2).\", \"mappings\": [{\"delta\": \"SD-86d15cb2\", \"basis\": \"D1\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The ADR amendment records D1 (R1, R2): a done sole-member spec keeps the gate criterion only when its governing sealed bundle carries it, and gets a blocker when sealed history is unreadable; it also records D2 (R4, R5): no checkpoint for a stop on an unknown read view of a done scope.\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F3\", \"rationale\": \"The ADR is amended to match runtime behaviour and the changelog exists, but the closeout skill amendment the spec plans was not made (F3).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\", \"rationale\": \"Remediation text is actionable on both success and removal failure, but the already-done branch reclassifies any blocked verify under a non-current view as unstable inputs, replacing plan.NextAction (F1); the hand-built path in the text is latent-divergent (F5).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R1-R6 each have named, passing tests in the trace; R4's loop wiring lacks an end-to-end test, declared in Known gaps and recorded as F2.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the change set's files with the spec's Artifacts list: they match one-to-one; review-brief changes in the commit range belong to a separate spec and are outside this change set.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Retaining a criterion only adds a requirement; it is keyed on the sealed plan, so no approval is created or widened; checkpoint removal uses the store path under the write guard; no secrets handled.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df\", \"rationale\": \"D1 rejects the smaller 'add to every done spec' option because it would supersede approvals; D2 avoids recording rather than deleting after the fact. ~80 lines of production code, no new extensibility. Invalidated if a done spec sealed with the gate still reads superseded or a stop's progress cannot be recovered from the repository.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan --strict\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it: 10 claims, 17 observed, no errors; the 909 findings are all orphan warnings about other tracked files in the repository, none about this change.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df\", \"rationale\": \"Not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands; relied on the sealed design assessment structure:design-67089a7abd53b9df.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended, not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands; discovery was done by reading the diff and the changed code.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended, not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands; relied on the sealed integration evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended, not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it: exit 1 with 'lifecycle status is not done' and next action 'record or remediate a fresh review'. That is the expected state before review and closeout, not a defect in the change.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it: exit 1, approved=false and fresh=false because no review is recorded yet (this review supplies it); the read view is current and the only warnings are metadata/unmapped governance paths, none about the change.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended, not in this reviewer profile's allowed commands.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability\", \"rationale\": \"Ran it strictly: 1 target, 194 results, 0 findings; sealed reachability of the closeout plan passes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Per the brief, did not rerun the full matrix; the sealed strict matrix run passes, and I reran the focused tests of the changed code with -race (all pass).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/done-spec-keeps-its-sealed-plan-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed module run of pose-mcp passes, including build:pose-mcp/go/build and the spec's own integration check; focused tests rerun locally pass.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1005,"type":"result","duration_ms":381931,"uuid":"34982f04-ccaa-498d-abad-c8693d50c780","ttft_stream_ms":905,"time_to_request_ms":43,"first_content_frame_ms":905,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":13061,"cacheReadInputTokens":270658,"cacheCreationInputTokens":41437,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6469196,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3324,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":41437,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-04T10:05:09.044Z"}
